      "src": "logos/ubuntu.svg",
      "alt": "Ubuntu logo",
      "width": 180,
      "height": 180
    },
    "pros": [
      "Five years of free security updates on the 26.04.1 LTS, until April 2031.",
      "The 26.10 interim brings GNOME 51 and Linux 7.3, including an amd64v3 desktop build.",
      "Server images for amd64, arm64, ppc64el, s390x and RISC-V in both releases.",
      "One installer family and one set of release notes per release."
    ],
    "cons": [
      "Desktop wants 6 GB RAM and 25 GB of free disk; below that Canonical recommends Xubuntu or Lubuntu.",
      "The 26.10 interim is supported for nine months only, until July 2027.",
      "The erase-disk option takes the entire selected drive; keeping another system means manual partitioning.",
      "Writing the stick erases it, and the running system’s own disk appears in the same device list."
    ],
